course: dictionary
lesson: 702
title: Words from church
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special place, such as church. They are not hard because they are clever. They just have their own meaning there. Context clues help you find it. Read the words around the word, then ask what would fit.
explain: «John the Baptist baptised him in the river Jordan.» Baptised is a doing word, and the water and the river are the clues. In church, baptise means to give someone the Christian ceremony of baptism, pouring water on them or putting them in water.
explain: Some words sound alike but mean different things. Christen is another way to say a person is given a name at their baptism. Being baptised is also a sign of joining Christ and the Church. Always check the clues to see which meaning fits.
fact: «Baptise» is a verb, so it shows an action. Its other forms are baptises, baptised and baptising.
fact: In the US, the spelling is baptize.
fact: A priest or minister baptises people in church.
fact: Some churches baptise babies, and some baptise only people old enough to choose. Christians disagree about this.
fact: «Christen» means to give someone a name at their baptism.
exercise: «John the Baptist baptised him in the river Jordan.» What does baptised mean here? | Gave him a new coat | Took him to the desert | *Gave him the Christian ceremony of baptism with water | Sang a song to him
exercise: «Baptists and many Pentecostal churches baptise people old enough to decide, usually by full immersion.» What does full immersion mean? | Singing loudly together | Being sprinkled with a few drops | Sitting quietly in a chair | *Going right under the water
exercise: In church, who can baptise someone? | *A priest or minister | A bus driver | A cook at the school | A football coach
test: «Whether to baptise babies or only believers is a disputed question among Christians.» What does disputed mean? | Forgotten long ago | Agreed on by everyone | *Argued about, with people disagreeing | Painted in bright colours
test: Which word means to give someone a name at their baptism? | Swim | Pray | Sing | *Christen
exam: What does baptise mean in «Christians call every child a gift from God and baptise babies or thank God for them»? | To count the children in a class | To wash the car on a sunny day | To send a letter to a friend | *To give the Christian ceremony of baptism, with water
